WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.514 --> 00:00:10.562
<font color="#00ff00" face="Monotype Corsiva">By</font>
<font color="#ff0000" face="Comic Sans MS" size="18">ongoL</font>

2
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:28.397
Thank you very kindly.

3
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:32.232
Ladies and gentlemen,
right now we'd like to introduce...

4
00:00:32.318 --> 00:00:36.988
the star of our show, the young man
you've all been waiting for.

5
00:00:37.073 --> 00:00:41.242
So let's all get together and welcome
him to the stage with a great big hand.

6
00:00:41.286 --> 00:00:43.453
How about it for Sam Cooke?

7
00:00:52.256 --> 00:00:55.841
Before we do anything, we'd like
to say how are you doing out there?

8
00:00:57.845 --> 00:00:59.595
- Is everyone feeling all right?
- Yeah!

9
00:00:59.681 --> 00:01:01.222
How are you doing?

10
00:01:02.142 --> 00:01:03.933
- You doing okay?
- Yeah!

11
00:01:03.976 --> 00:01:06.393
- You two doing okay?
- Yeah!

12
00:01:06.437 --> 00:01:10.231
Well, I ask you one more time.
How you doing?

13
00:01:11.984 --> 00:01:13.942
Oh, yeah

14
00:01:15.113 --> 00:01:16.988
I said oh, yeah

15
00:01:17.074 --> 00:01:19.074
Oh, yeah!

16
00:01:19.160 --> 00:01:20.618
Oh, yeah

17
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:22.243
Oh, yeah!

18
00:01:30.087 --> 00:01:33.213
I believe we're gonna have
a goodtime tonight

19
00:01:34.467 --> 00:01:38.177
It's good to have somebody
you can twist the night away with

20
00:01:38.261 --> 00:01:40.344
Right now

21
00:01:40.431 --> 00:01:41.805
Oh, yes, it is

22
00:01:42.683 --> 00:01:46.060
I said it feels good
when you got somebody

23
00:01:46.146 --> 00:01:48.730
To twist the night away
with right now

24
00:01:48.815 --> 00:01:51.149
- Lord have mercy.
- What you running from, son?

25
00:01:53.863 --> 00:01:55.446
We got a call.

26
00:02:01.495 --> 00:02:04.955
Don't fight the feelin'
Don’t fight the feelin'

27
00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:09.752
Got to feel the feelin' now
Got to feel the feelin'

28
00:02:10.839 --> 00:02:14.341
'Cause it make you groove right
when you feel the feelin'

29
00:02:14.425 --> 00:02:17.676
Oh, make me want you now

30
00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:20.095
Got to feel the feelin'

31
00:02:20.182 --> 00:02:24.894
'Cause it make you groove right
when you feel the feelin'

32
00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:29.564
Make me want ya
when I got the feelin; baby

33
00:02:29.650 --> 00:02:31.859
So don't fight it

34
00:02:31.943 --> 00:02:33.860
No, don’t fight it

35
00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:36.530
Baby, just feel it

36
00:03:30.505 --> 00:03:32.547
I'm gonna bust you up.

37
00:03:32.591 --> 00:03:35.217
Beat your ass
like I was your daddy.

38
00:04:16.888 --> 00:04:19.973
I said I'm beginning
to feel alright now

39
00:04:25.981 --> 00:04:29.983
I feel can tell you
about my baby right now

40
00:04:34.115 --> 00:04:37.158
I said I feel
you're in the mood right now

41
00:04:45.877 --> 00:04:49.379
I said I feel
you're in the mood

42
00:04:51.925 --> 00:04:54.342
Sometimes me and my baby
we fuss and fight

43
00:04:54.428 --> 00:04:57.346
And my baby leave home
'cause things ain't right

44
00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.847
For those of you
who think you came here today...

45
00:04:59.891 --> 00:05:02.642
to hear us tell you
like these Negro leaders do...

46
00:05:02.686 --> 00:05:05.312
that your times
will just get better...

47
00:05:05.397 --> 00:05:10.401
that we shall
overcome someday...

48
00:05:10.486 --> 00:05:13.529
I say to you,
you came to the wrong place.

49
00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:16.906
Because your times will never
get better unless you make them better.

50
00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:21.036
Those of you who think you came here
to hear us tell you...

51
00:05:21.081 --> 00:05:24.708
to turn the other cheek
to the brutality of the white man...

52
00:05:24.792 --> 00:05:28.669
and this system of injustice
that's in place right here in America...

53
00:05:28.714 --> 00:05:31.089
you think you're gonna come here
and hear us tell you...

54
00:05:31.173 --> 00:05:35.175
to go out there and beg
for a place at their lunch counter...

55
00:05:35.971 --> 00:05:39.181
again, I say you came
to the wrong place.

56
00:05:39.225 --> 00:05:43.686
We don't teach you
to turn the other cheek in the South.

57
00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:46.522
And we don't teach you
to turn the other cheek in the North.

58
00:05:46.566 --> 00:05:50.402
The Honorable Elijah Muhammad
teaches you to obey the law...

59
00:05:50.444 --> 00:05:53.237
to Cary yourselves
in a respectable way...

60
00:05:53.322 --> 00:05:55.864
in a proud
Afro-American way.

61
00:05:56.576 --> 00:05:59.118
But at the same time,
we teach you...

62
00:05:59.203 --> 00:06:01.537
that anyone puts
their hand on you...

63
00:06:03.667 --> 00:06:08.796
brother, you do your best to see they
don't put their hand on anybody else...

64
00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:10.129
again.

65
00:06:14.595 --> 00:06:15.927
Time.

66
00:06:35.325 --> 00:06:37.283
Just like that, Daddy.

67
00:06:37.327 --> 00:06:39.410
Never jump in one place.
Bad for the heart.

68
00:06:39.455 --> 00:06:41.038
Forwards, backwards, sideways.

69
00:06:41.124 --> 00:06:42.999
That's the most important thing.

70
00:06:54.136 --> 00:06:56.261
I'm called Bundini.

71
00:06:56.348 --> 00:06:59.891
Rhymes with Houdini.
He was a Jew too.

72
00:06:59.977 --> 00:07:03.687
Some people call me Fast Black.
Some call me Daddy Mac.

73
00:07:04.814 --> 00:07:07.523
Gave Sugar Ray Robinson
my power for seven years.

74
00:07:07.609 --> 00:07:10.068
My voodoo. My magic.

75
00:07:10.153 --> 00:07:13.071
Now Shorty done sent me here
to work for you.

76
00:07:13.157 --> 00:07:16.367
- Who's Shorty?
- I call him Shorty.

77
00:07:16.452 --> 00:07:18.619
Call him Shorty
'cause he like 'em circumcised.

78
00:07:18.703 --> 00:07:23.498
Original people. Like Moses.
And I was a babe in a basket too.

79
00:07:23.584 --> 00:07:26.752
Born on a doorstep with a note
across my chest that read...

80
00:07:26.838 --> 00:07:29.881
"You do the best
you can for him, world. "

81
00:07:29.966 --> 00:07:31.883
I wanna be your inspiration.

82
00:07:31.968 --> 00:07:34.635
Your motivator in your corner.

83
00:07:35.806 --> 00:07:38.098
Can I be in your corner,
young man?

84
00:07:45.525 --> 00:07:46.941
Time!

85
00:07:50.363 --> 00:07:53.281
Got to tell you
how I feel right now

86
00:07:53.366 --> 00:07:56.200
This song gonna tell you
howl feel

87
00:07:56.285 --> 00:07:59.662
I know you been gone away
for along time, but listen

88
00:07:59.705 --> 00:08:02.331
Baby, if you ever

89
00:08:03.584 --> 00:08:06.543
Change your mind

90
00:08:06.630 --> 00:08:08.839
Know that leaving

91
00:08:08.882 --> 00:08:11.716
Leaving me behind

92
00:08:13.386 --> 00:08:14.635
Bring it tome

93
00:08:15.347 --> 00:08:17.848
Bring that good lovin; baby

94
00:08:17.933 --> 00:08:20.058
Bring it on home to me

95
00:08:20.144 --> 00:08:21.476
Yeah, yeah

96
00:08:21.561 --> 00:08:25.230
Listen, I got to be a man
to tell you this, honey, look

97
00:08:25.316 --> 00:08:27.358
I'll give you jewelry

98
00:08:27.444 --> 00:08:29.486
I'll give you some
of that money too

99
00:08:29.571 --> 00:08:32.155
But listen
That ain't all

100
00:08:32.239 --> 00:08:34.948
That ain't all
Sam will do for you

101
00:08:35.034 --> 00:08:38.285
All you got to do
is bring it tome

102
00:08:39.081 --> 00:08:41.290
Bring that good lovin baby

103
00:08:41.374 --> 00:08:43.332
Be the invisible man
as soon as he swings.

104
00:08:43.418 --> 00:08:45.126
Get personal with him.

105
00:08:45.212 --> 00:08:47.629
This is important
Listen tome

106
00:08:47.715 --> 00:08:50.925
Don't you know
that I'll always

107
00:08:51.009 --> 00:08:53.009
I'll always be your slave

108
00:08:54.388 --> 00:08:56.763
Till I'm buried

109
00:08:56.850 --> 00:08:59.225
Buried in my grave

110
00:08:59.268 --> 00:09:01.310
While I'm livin'

111
00:09:01.396 --> 00:09:04.606
Bring it tome
Bring that good lovin; baby

112
00:09:05.401 --> 00:09:07.985
Bring it on home to me

113
00:09:08.069 --> 00:09:10.027
One more thing
I gotta tell you

114
00:09:10.113 --> 00:09:11.821
Listen to me right now

115
00:09:11.907 --> 00:09:15.117
You know that I try

116
00:09:15.161 --> 00:09:18.246
To treat you right
What did you do

117
00:09:18.330 --> 00:09:20.330
You stayed up

118
00:09:20.416 --> 00:09:22.625
You stayed up late at night

119
00:09:22.710 --> 00:09:24.668
I don't care
who you was with

120
00:09:24.753 --> 00:09:26.628
Bring it tome

121
00:09:26.713 --> 00:09:29.297
Bring all that good lovin; baby

122
00:09:29.383 --> 00:09:32.468
Bring it on
Everybody's with me

123
00:09:32.554 --> 00:09:33.970
Everybody's with me tonight

124
00:09:34.055 --> 00:09:37.390
Listen, let me hear you
say yeah

125
00:09:44.107 --> 00:09:46.733
Yeah, oh, yeah

126
00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:54.616
Sonny Liston,
you ain't no champ! You a chump!

127
00:09:54.702 --> 00:09:56.827
Float like a butterfly,
sting like a bee.

128
00:09:56.913 --> 00:09:59.914
Oh!
Rumble, young man, rumble.

129
00:09:59.998 --> 00:10:02.749
Y'all wanna lose y' all money?
Then you bet it on Sonny.

130
00:10:02.835 --> 00:10:05.669
He know I'm great.
He will fall in eight.

131
00:10:05.755 --> 00:10:08.506
Come on, you big, ugly bear.
I'll whup you right now.

132
00:10:10.218 --> 00:10:13.595
Two-ten and a half.
Two-ten and a half!

133
00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:17.474
The challenger, Cassius Clay,
two hundred and ten and a half pounds.

134
00:10:17.518 --> 00:10:20.144
- Man, you sure that's right?
- That's what the weight is.

135
00:10:20.228 --> 00:10:22.812
Old, ugly bear, come on.
Let's go.

136
00:10:22.898 --> 00:10:27.359
You got these folks fooled. I ain't
scared of ya! I ain't scared of ya!

137
00:10:29.154 --> 00:10:31.446
Two hundred and eighteen.
Two hundred and eighteen.

138
00:10:31.532 --> 00:10:34.408
Sonny Liston,
the champion of the world.

139
00:10:34.494 --> 00:10:36.786
Two hundred and eighteen pounds.

140
00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:38.912
- Pounds of what?
- Pounds of ugly.

141
00:10:38.998 --> 00:10:41.499
That man's so ugly,
when he sweat...

142
00:10:41.584 --> 00:10:45.378
the sweat run backwards off his forehand
just to stay away from his face.

143
00:10:49.885 --> 00:10:52.594
Come on, you big, ugly bear!
I'll turn you into a rug!

144
00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:55.139
Keep talkin'.
I'm gonna fuck you up.

145
00:11:01.689 --> 00:11:03.105
If you whup me...

146
00:11:03.190 --> 00:11:07.109
I'll crawl out of the ring and take
the first jet airplane out the country.

147
00:11:07.195 --> 00:11:10.321
- Is that a promise, Mr. Clay?
- You'll eat his words first.

148
00:11:10.407 --> 00:11:14.243
- Cassius, you're a 7-1 underdog.
- Liston says he talks with his fists.

149
00:11:14.285 --> 00:11:16.285
- What do you say?
- You scared of him?

150
00:11:16.371 --> 00:11:18.621
I'm gonna give Sonny Liston
talkin' lessons...

151
00:11:18.707 --> 00:11:21.166
boxin' lessons
and fallin' down lessons.

152
00:11:21.960 --> 00:11:25.086
Cassius, are you a black Muslim?
Pat Putnam says in the Miami Herald--

153
00:11:25.172 --> 00:11:27.714
A man's religion is his own business.
What kind of question is that?

154
00:11:27.759 --> 00:11:33.013
- Angelo, tell me--
- Malcolm X was in town, then he left.

155
00:11:33.097 --> 00:11:35.222
Was that so
he wouldn't embarrass you?

156
00:11:35.308 --> 00:11:37.183
- Yeah, Howard?
- Liston doesn't like you.

157
00:11:37.268 --> 00:11:40.102
Really can't stand you.
Says he wants to kill you.

158
00:11:40.146 --> 00:11:42.229
Howard Cosell, you ain't
nothin' but an instigator.

159
00:11:42.315 --> 00:11:45.900
- Man, how you get that way?
- Cassius, now you’re being truculent.

160
00:11:45.986 --> 00:11:47.444
If it's good, I'm that.

161
00:11:49.947 --> 00:11:53.574
You next. Soon as I'm done with Sonny
Liston, I'm fightin' Howard Cosell.

162
00:11:53.660 --> 00:11:55.618
Y'all write that down right now.

163
00:12:10.761 --> 00:12:12.469
That's good?

164
00:12:13.515 --> 00:12:15.098
Wanna check that out?

165
00:12:23.482 --> 00:12:25.816
Hey, man, when you get back?

166
00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:28.653
I just got here.
I'm front row, seat seven.

167
00:12:32.701 --> 00:12:35.368
I'll be sittin'
with Mom and Dad.

168
00:12:38.208 --> 00:12:41.793
You should've stayed in the first place.
Nobody gotta hide when they're with me.

169
00:12:41.877 --> 00:12:44.211
There's nothing wrong
with being cool, my brother.

170
00:12:44.296 --> 00:12:45.211
He's right.

171
00:13:32.723 --> 00:13:35.349
- ...and challenger, Cassius Clay.
- Good evening, ladies and gentlemen.

172
00:13:35.391 --> 00:13:38.726
Brought to you
by the City Service Oil Company...

173
00:13:38.812 --> 00:13:42.189
and its dealers
in 37 states and Canada...

174
00:13:42.233 --> 00:13:45.651
known to millions of motorists
for Big Gallon gasoline...

175
00:13:45.736 --> 00:13:49.488
and by new Wildroot,
totally new Wildroot in a new tube...

176
00:13:49.574 --> 00:13:54.661
with a great formula that grooms hair
to look neat and natural, never greasy.

177
00:13:54.745 --> 00:13:57.079
Another boxing milestone
is at hand.

178
00:13:57.165 --> 00:14:01.084
In just a few minutes,
Louisville's Cassius Marcellus Clay...

179
00:14:01.128 --> 00:14:03.253
will be facing
the devastating punching power...

180
00:14:03.338 --> 00:14:06.589
of the heavyweight champion,
Charles "Sonny" Liston.

181
00:14:06.634 --> 00:14:10.803
...for the heavyweight championship
of the world.

182
00:14:13.265 --> 00:14:15.265
Introducing, on my right--

183
00:14:16.227 --> 00:14:18.227
And now the time has come.

184
00:14:18.313 --> 00:14:22.899
Both challenger and champion
are in the ring.

185
00:14:22.942 --> 00:14:26.402
The heavyweight championship
of the world is on the line.

186
00:14:26.488 --> 00:14:30.282
I fit goes past the first round,
there will be surprises already.

187
00:14:30.992 --> 00:14:34.452
Sonny Liston wrapped in that
tery cloth towel of his...

188
00:14:34.538 --> 00:14:37.205
wrapped around his head
swami fashion...

189
00:14:37.291 --> 00:14:40.125
Looking as malevolent
and baleful as ever.

190
00:14:40.169 --> 00:14:43.546
But this man
is a professional prizefighter.

191
00:14:43.631 --> 00:14:45.673
Make no mistake about it.

192
00:14:48.844 --> 00:14:50.802
I want a clean fight.

193
00:14:50.846 --> 00:14:53.263
When I say break,
stop punching and step back.

194
00:14:53.308 --> 00:14:55.433
Do you have
any questions, champ?

195
00:14:55.519 --> 00:14:57.352
Any questions, challenger?

196
00:14:57.437 --> 00:15:01.189
We're fine.
Touch gloves, gentlemen. Good luck.

197
00:15:04.195 --> 00:15:06.988
Good evening,
sports fans across the nation.

198
00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:09.656
Liston in the white trunks
with the black stripes.

199
00:15:09.741 --> 00:15:13.869
Clay, an inch and a half taller, in
the white trunks with the red stripes--

200
00:15:27.969 --> 00:15:30.762
And Cassius Clay
is sidestepping.

201
00:15:45.404 --> 00:15:47.738
There it is, champ.
Stay on your toes now.

202
00:15:55.624 --> 00:15:59.376
And we can see that the champion
is the aggressor.

203
00:15:59.418 --> 00:16:02.002
There's a shot under the heart.

204
00:16:30.994 --> 00:16:34.412
Cassius Clay slips away.
And now Clay pounds a left.

205
00:16:34.497 --> 00:16:37.498
Another left. A straight jab.

206
00:16:41.005 --> 00:16:43.798
It seems to have stunned him.
And that's the bell.

207
00:16:43.882 --> 00:16:47.300
And they're fighting after the bell.
And they're still fighting.

208
00:16:47.386 --> 00:16:49.970
This round is over.

209
00:16:50.056 --> 00:16:51.847
Break it up, ref.

210
00:16:51.934 --> 00:16:55.019
There is no love lost between
the two contenders at this time.

211
00:16:55.102 --> 00:16:58.938
Cassius goes back to his corner.
It's been an amazing round.

212
00:16:58.982 --> 00:17:00.481
You can beat this guy.

213
00:17:02.986 --> 00:17:05.487
I'm still here.

214
00:17:05.572 --> 00:17:08.949
And Sonny Liston
is not taking the stool.

215
00:17:08.993 --> 00:17:12.036
He's anxious to get back
into the challenger's face.

216
00:17:12.120 --> 00:17:15.038
Take it to the body.
Kill the body, the head will follow.

217
00:17:46.114 --> 00:17:48.406
This is a totally different fight
than Liston expected...

218
00:17:48.492 --> 00:17:50.325
and anyone in this arena
will tell you.

219
00:17:50.411 --> 00:17:54.789
There's a long, looping left hand.
Clay's eyes are wide open now.

220
00:18:05.509 --> 00:18:07.843
- Come on, Cass! Move!
- Step back.

221
00:18:09.848 --> 00:18:12.724
- Come on, Cassius!
- Come on, Chi-Chi!

222
00:18:15.771 --> 00:18:17.437
I'm not prognosticating
anything...

223
00:18:17.523 --> 00:18:19.857
but merely his survival
to this juncture--

224
00:18:37.586 --> 00:18:39.544
Cass, hit him!

225
00:18:50.724 --> 00:18:51.639
Break.

226
00:18:53.144 --> 00:18:54.977
Let him go.

227
00:19:23.426 --> 00:19:27.095
Sonny Liston is hurt.
He's bleeding from his eye.

228
00:19:30.058 --> 00:19:31.390
He's defying the experts early.

229
00:19:31.434 --> 00:19:36.312
We have to take a look at this man and
say he is not in awe of the champion.

230
00:20:04.719 --> 00:20:08.179
He ain't nothin' to me.
And he know it.

231
00:20:08.265 --> 00:20:09.681
This is it now.

232
00:20:15.647 --> 00:20:17.605
Let me have that, John.

233
00:20:22.655 --> 00:20:24.279
And now they're ready.

234
00:20:28.493 --> 00:20:31.035
You gonna knock
the ugly off of him.

235
00:20:31.121 --> 00:20:33.371
That's gonna take a long time,
but you can do it.

236
00:20:37.503 --> 00:20:39.795
There he is. Get him off.
Do your job, ref.

237
00:20:40.548 --> 00:20:42.923
Shake him.
Do your job, ref.

238
00:20:47.805 --> 00:20:49.972
There it is.

239
00:20:50.767 --> 00:20:52.350
Come on, ref.

240
00:20:56.231 --> 00:20:57.230
Break.

241
00:21:03.363 --> 00:21:05.780
- There he is.
- Clay slips around and out.

242
00:21:08.828 --> 00:21:11.495
Up against the ropes.
Right above me now.

243
00:21:15.627 --> 00:21:18.169
Too tight. Get in there.

244
00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.642
My eyes. There's something in my eyes.
I can't see nothin'.

245
00:21:32.728 --> 00:21:33.810
Come on.

246
00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.649
- What's going on?
- Nothin'.

247
00:21:38.735 --> 00:21:42.278
The guy's punchin' on the breaks.
Just take care of it. We're fine.

248
00:21:44.324 --> 00:21:46.699
I can't see nothin', man.
Just go and cut 'em off, Angie.

249
00:21:46.743 --> 00:21:49.577
No, no. You can't fight
with no gloves on.

250
00:21:50.413 --> 00:21:52.371
Just get up. Get up.
Try and do it. Come on.

251
00:21:52.416 --> 00:21:54.875
I can't see, man.

252
00:21:54.919 --> 00:21:57.586
- Come on, Cass!
- Dance!

253
00:22:04.262 --> 00:22:06.262
Liston crouching,
hitting to the body.

254
00:22:06.346 --> 00:22:09.305
It's like he's blinking,
like he doesn't see Liston.

255
00:22:09.392 --> 00:22:11.976
Ref, you gotta do your job.

256
00:22:21.697 --> 00:22:22.737
Hold it.

257
00:22:25.742 --> 00:22:28.117
Stay away from him, Clay.
Stay away from him.

258
00:22:28.913 --> 00:22:31.288
The champion, you can see,
is the aggressor.

259
00:22:37.755 --> 00:22:39.672
- Get him, Cass!
- Come on, Cass!

260
00:22:40.758 --> 00:22:43.259
- Knock him up!
- Clay looks all done.

261
00:22:43.344 --> 00:22:45.344
Hold on to him!

262
00:22:49.560 --> 00:22:52.353
- Stop it. Stop. Break.
- Knock him up.

263
00:22:55.732 --> 00:22:58.149
Get on him.
Get on him, man.

264
00:23:15.336 --> 00:23:18.295
- You can see him now.
- You go get him, man.

265
00:23:29.434 --> 00:23:31.935
Clay lands a left,
but Liston ducked under it...

266
00:23:32.020 --> 00:23:34.270
and took it high
on the forehead.

267
00:23:35.233 --> 00:23:37.442
It's Clay coming on.

268
00:23:42.365 --> 00:23:45.074
And Liston backs away.

269
00:24:30.749 --> 00:24:34.459
And all the predictions
are going down the drain...

270
00:24:34.545 --> 00:24:36.462
as Liston is listless.

271
00:24:38.840 --> 00:24:40.631
And there's the bell.

272
00:24:43.554 --> 00:24:45.471
We're coming up
to round seven.

273
00:25:23.804 --> 00:25:26.138
Wait a minute!

274
00:25:26.224 --> 00:25:28.015
Liston's not coming out.

275
00:25:29.019 --> 00:25:32.312
The winner and new heavyweight
champion of the world is Cassius Clay.

276
00:25:32.396 --> 00:25:36.440
Eat your words!
Eat your words!

277
00:25:36.485 --> 00:25:40.279
Les, I'm going up into the ring.
Get back.

278
00:25:41.490 --> 00:25:43.865
I'm the greatest thing
ever happened to boxing.

279
00:25:43.951 --> 00:25:45.784
Cassius. Cassius.

280
00:25:45.828 --> 00:25:48.412
I shook up the world!

281
00:25:48.498 --> 00:25:51.749
It's a scene of
absolute bedlam in the ring!

282
00:25:51.834 --> 00:25:56.087
I am the greatest.
I'm a bad man. I shook up the world!

283
00:25:56.172 --> 00:25:57.880
Did he ever hurt you?

284
00:25:57.966 --> 00:26:00.967
I'm only 22 years old.
I ain't got a mark on my face.

285
00:26:01.010 --> 00:26:02.968
- I must be the greatest.
- And you're pretty.

286
00:26:03.013 --> 00:26:04.971
I must be the greatest.

287
00:26:05.015 --> 00:26:08.308
Wait. Hold on. Hold on one second.
That's Sam Cooke back there.

288
00:26:08.351 --> 00:26:10.309
- Come on, Sam Cooke.
- Let Sam Cooke in here.

289
00:26:10.353 --> 00:26:13.271
The greatest rock-and-roll singer,
and I'm the world's greatest boxer.

290
00:26:13.357 --> 00:26:14.856
Hello, Sam.

291
00:26:23.785 --> 00:26:25.952
That mummy's
gonna get him, baby.

292
00:26:26.787 --> 00:26:29.204
- That mummy ain't gonna get him.
- Yeah, he is.

293
00:26:29.290 --> 00:26:33.543
He ain't scared of that mummy.
That mummy too slow to catch anybody.

294
00:26:34.505 --> 00:26:37.131
- What's going on, Sam?
- How you doing, Cassius?

295
00:26:37.215 --> 00:26:41.676
Don't believe that stuff on TV.
Don't listen to him.

296
00:26:41.721 --> 00:26:43.846
- Hey, congratulations, Clay.
- Hey, thank you, Jim.

297
00:26:43.930 --> 00:26:46.931
- Hell of a fight.
- You next, man. You next.

298
00:26:47.017 --> 00:26:50.310
- Go ahead and get some food, brother.
- Cassius Clay versus Jim Brown.

299
00:26:50.396 --> 00:26:51.812
Biggest fight in history.

300
00:26:51.898 --> 00:26:55.024
- The mummy only has one eye.
- One eye and a limp.

301
00:26:55.067 --> 00:26:57.693
That mummy's 643 years old.

302
00:26:57.737 --> 00:26:59.695
He can't catch nobody.
Look at him.

303
00:26:59.740 --> 00:27:02.950
You gotta fall down 'cause that's
the only way the mummy could catch you.

304
00:27:14.463 --> 00:27:15.921
Way to go, champ!

305
00:27:18.593 --> 00:27:22.011
- Yeah, you the greatest.
- Thank you, brother. Thank you.

306
00:27:22.095 --> 00:27:24.053
- I'll see your next fight.
- You'll see the next one?

307
00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:26.974
- Oh, yeah.
- Well, you better get there very early.

308
00:27:27.060 --> 00:27:30.061
You better get there very early
'cause that man's going down.

309
00:27:32.774 --> 00:27:35.400
If he talk a little jive,
he's going down in five.

310
00:27:37.321 --> 00:27:40.280
He talk a little more,
I might drop him in four.

311
00:27:41.408 --> 00:27:43.575
If you wanna have more fun,
do it in round one.

312
00:27:43.660 --> 00:27:45.743
Oh, yeah. Hold on.
I'm doing the rhymin'.

313
00:27:59.760 --> 00:28:03.011
The people really look up to you. You
plan on being a champ like Joe Louis?

314
00:28:03.098 --> 00:28:06.057
Well, yeah, I'm gonna be
the people's champ.

315
00:28:06.142 --> 00:28:08.517
Not like Joe Louis.
Well, you know, not exactly.

316
00:28:10.981 --> 00:28:13.106
My name is not Clay.

317
00:28:13.151 --> 00:28:15.735
Clay is the name of the people
that owned my ancestors...

318
00:28:15.819 --> 00:28:18.820
and I no longer wanna be called
by that slave name.

319
00:28:18.906 --> 00:28:21.156
- I am Cassius X.
- Minister Malcolm.

320
00:28:21.242 --> 00:28:23.492
What about the divisions
in the Nation of Islam?

321
00:28:23.577 --> 00:28:27.579
This is the champ's time. I'm here
as a friend to support his victory...

322
00:28:27.665 --> 00:28:30.124
so I have nothing you want.

323
00:28:30.168 --> 00:28:32.168
I'm definitely gonna be
the people's champion...

324
00:28:32.211 --> 00:28:34.670
but I just ain't gonna be the champ
the way you want me to be the champ.

325
00:28:34.755 --> 00:28:37.172
I'm gonna be the champ
the way I wanna be.

326
00:28:48.354 --> 00:28:50.980
...for no home is immune
to termites...

327
00:28:51.022 --> 00:28:54.148
no matter how well
it is built or maintained.

328
00:28:54.234 --> 00:28:56.192
- Hey, brother.
- I was leaving.

329
00:28:56.279 --> 00:28:59.530
I saw your light on.
What you doing up at this hour, champ?

330
00:28:59.615 --> 00:29:03.367
Oh, man, I'm watching this program
on termites.

331
00:29:03.453 --> 00:29:07.706
And them little itsy-bitsy things is
eatin' these people's whole house down.

332
00:29:07.790 --> 00:29:10.499
Oh, man, look.

333
00:29:13.630 --> 00:29:18.383
I've been invited to speak
at Ibadan University in Nigeria.

334
00:29:18.427 --> 00:29:21.136
- You wanna go with me?
- Hey, look, man.

335
00:29:21.222 --> 00:29:25.350
You can have six million termites
in your house and don't even know it...

336
00:29:25.391 --> 00:29:28.350
till you going to get something to eat
and you bust through the floor.

337
00:29:30.231 --> 00:29:33.983
- What'd you say? Where?
- Africa. You been?

338
00:29:35.069 --> 00:29:35.984
Africa.

339
00:29:36.070 --> 00:29:38.404
All right, come on.
Let's go.

340
00:29:43.994 --> 00:29:45.577
What is it?

341
00:29:50.085 --> 00:29:52.669
You ever thought
you'd lose it?

342
00:29:52.754 --> 00:29:55.505
I mean, really lose it?

343
00:29:59.346 --> 00:30:03.098
When I was little, I tore out
this picture of Emmett Till.

344
00:30:03.182 --> 00:30:05.099
They put the barbed wire
around his neck...

345
00:30:05.184 --> 00:30:09.353
and strapped him
to that 75-pound cotton gin fan.

346
00:30:09.439 --> 00:30:13.275
And they cut out one of his eyes
'cause he looked at some white lady.

347
00:30:15.112 --> 00:30:17.070
Man.

348
00:30:17.114 --> 00:30:20.199
I couldn't take my eyes to it,
couldn't throw it away.

349
00:30:24.788 --> 00:30:27.706
When I heard about those...

350
00:30:27.791 --> 00:30:30.750
four little girls who got bombed
in that Birmingham church...

351
00:30:33.965 --> 00:30:36.674
the prohibitions of the Honorable
Elijah Muhammad prevented me...

352
00:30:36.758 --> 00:30:39.008
from speaking
my thoughts in action.

353
00:30:41.013 --> 00:30:43.222
Because Birmingham was part
of the civil rights struggle.

354
00:30:43.308 --> 00:30:47.519
You know, begging for our place
at the white man's table.

355
00:30:47.604 --> 00:30:50.271
But dead children
are dead children.

356
00:30:50.357 --> 00:30:54.902
So the anger I felt
I had to contain.

357
00:30:56.821 --> 00:30:59.906
I locked it up so tight...

358
00:30:59.992 --> 00:31:01.909
my muscles seized.

359
00:31:03.079 --> 00:31:05.997
I lost control
over the right side of my body.

360
00:31:06.082 --> 00:31:08.499
My leg gave out.

361
00:31:08.585 --> 00:31:11.294
Right arm gave out.
"I'm having a stroke," I thought.

362
00:31:12.880 --> 00:31:16.006
But I had to hold it in
'cause all I wanted--

363
00:31:16.092 --> 00:31:20.553
Brother, all I wanted to do
was find something and break it.

364
00:31:20.639 --> 00:31:23.807
Break a part--
Break any part of this system...

365
00:31:23.892 --> 00:31:28.103
because you are so provoked
in your heart...

366
00:31:28.189 --> 00:31:30.314
and your spirit
as a human being...

367
00:31:32.234 --> 00:31:34.192
at dead children.

368
00:31:35.863 --> 00:31:37.946
And I could do...

369
00:31:40.534 --> 00:31:42.284
nothing.

370
00:31:50.711 --> 00:31:54.463
Everyone knows
I can't do nothing...

371
00:31:54.549 --> 00:31:55.965
anymore.

372
00:32:00.472 --> 00:32:04.015
So Elijah Muhammad has suspended me
as a minister in the Nation of Islam.

373
00:32:12.527 --> 00:32:15.361
Man...

374
00:32:15.404 --> 00:32:16.945
you can fix that.

375
00:32:17.031 --> 00:32:19.907
I don't know.

376
00:32:19.951 --> 00:32:22.243
I'll try when we get back.

377
00:32:30.462 --> 00:32:32.504
You get some rest, champ.

378
00:32:32.590 --> 00:32:34.507
All right, brother.

379
00:33:09.795 --> 00:33:10.752
Sit.

380
00:33:23.143 --> 00:33:27.771
You know, only after
long service and high merit...

381
00:33:27.814 --> 00:33:32.275
in the spiritual and physical rebirth
of Afro-American people...

382
00:33:32.319 --> 00:33:34.569
is one granted an original name.

383
00:33:34.656 --> 00:33:37.407
But you are special.

384
00:33:37.490 --> 00:33:38.948
A world champion.

385
00:33:41.495 --> 00:33:44.121
So there is a gift
I wish to give you.

386
00:33:44.165 --> 00:33:46.165
From this day forward...

387
00:33:46.208 --> 00:33:50.711
you will be known
as Muhammad Ali.

388
00:33:54.884 --> 00:33:57.259
- What?
- That's right.

389
00:33:57.345 --> 00:33:59.262
You what?

390
00:34:01.767 --> 00:34:05.477
Well, what's wrong with our name?
My name?

391
00:34:05.521 --> 00:34:07.855
We-- We made you.

392
00:34:07.940 --> 00:34:09.398
Ain't nobody made me.

393
00:34:09.484 --> 00:34:11.609
No bow tie-wearin',
Arab-talkin' nigger gonna change that.

394
00:34:11.693 --> 00:34:13.610
Ain't nobody in that ring but me.
I made me.

395
00:34:13.695 --> 00:34:16.196
You don't know who you are.

396
00:34:16.282 --> 00:34:19.033
I know who I ain't.
I ain't drinkin'.

397
00:34:19.119 --> 00:34:21.411
I ain't going back on my wife
and for sure I ain't prayin'...

398
00:34:21.495 --> 00:34:23.662
to no blond-haired,
blue-eyed Jesus.

399
00:34:23.706 --> 00:34:27.667
Paintin' those blue-eyed, blond-haired
Jesuses is what put food in you.

400
00:34:27.753 --> 00:34:30.420
- Steak and vegetables on the table.
- It's dinner!

401
00:34:36.053 --> 00:34:37.970
Go ahead.

402
00:34:39.097 --> 00:34:40.429
Go ahead.

403
00:35:02.373 --> 00:35:03.622
Hello?

404
00:35:04.542 --> 00:35:07.084
Here you go, Daddy.

405
00:35:07.168 --> 00:35:08.709
Thank you, baby.

406
00:35:08.753 --> 00:35:11.212
- Yeah?
- Brother Malcolm.

407
00:35:11.256 --> 00:35:15.300
The Honorable Elijah Muhammad has given
the Muslim name of Muhammad Ali...

408
00:35:15.385 --> 00:35:18.136
to Cassius X.

409
00:35:18.222 --> 00:35:21.640
Herbert Muhammad has been put
in charge of his training.

410
00:35:21.727 --> 00:35:23.977
He will not be traveling
with you to Africa.

411
00:35:24.061 --> 00:35:26.687
He also asked me
to inform you...

412
00:35:26.772 --> 00:35:29.773
that your suspension
will be extended indefinitely.

413
00:35:40.413 --> 00:35:42.872
Brother Cassius
won't be coming to Africa.

414
00:35:46.460 --> 00:35:48.418
Not with me.

415
00:35:52.383 --> 00:35:54.508
Don't put it off.

416
00:35:59.765 --> 00:36:01.682
We'll be fine.

417
00:36:06.815 --> 00:36:08.189
I will.

418
00:36:08.274 --> 00:36:11.442
I got a little doll
for Atallah.

419
00:36:11.487 --> 00:36:12.569
Really?

420
00:36:12.655 --> 00:36:14.279
Yeah, it’s beautiful.

421
00:36:14.323 --> 00:36:17.157
I've got so much
to show the girls when I get back.

422
00:36:17.200 --> 00:36:19.617
- I'm taking a lot of pictures.
- Yeah?

423
00:36:19.661 --> 00:36:21.995
Yeah, I got some good stuff
I want to show you.

424
00:36:22.081 --> 00:36:23.998
Are you eating?

425
00:36:25.001 --> 00:36:27.585
Well, you're not cooking, so--

426
00:36:27.670 --> 00:36:30.296
- What's going on? Anything?
- Nothing.

427
00:36:31.258 --> 00:36:33.383
He's on the phone,
talking to his wife.

428
00:36:33.469 --> 00:36:36.637
She's having a hard time sleeping,
the baby's kicking a lot...

429
00:36:36.721 --> 00:36:39.013
what are they gonna
name the baby.

430
00:36:41.852 --> 00:36:45.896
I just wake up a couple of times
in the night, but it’s okay.

431
00:36:58.494 --> 00:37:00.869
Would you like to take a seat?

432
00:37:00.914 --> 00:37:02.872
Sure, thank you.

433
00:37:06.545 --> 00:37:08.754
What y'all done did
with the real pilot?

434
00:37:08.839 --> 00:37:11.715
I am the pilot.
He's the copilot.

435
00:37:11.757 --> 00:37:13.715
Here. Sit down, Mr. Clay.

436
00:37:13.760 --> 00:37:16.177
Oh, man.

437
00:37:16.221 --> 00:37:20.182
In Louisville, where I growed up,
they barely let black folks drive buses.

438
00:38:59.997 --> 00:39:01.246
Muhammad!

439
00:39:04.711 --> 00:39:08.505
Hey, brother.
What's going on, man?

440
00:39:12.678 --> 00:39:14.636
- What you doing here?
- I was just going to the airport.

441
00:39:14.680 --> 00:39:17.306
We just got here now.
So where you going?

442
00:39:17.348 --> 00:39:18.305
Liberia.

443
00:39:18.349 --> 00:39:21.809
Say hello to Maya Angelou right here
and Ambassador Huang Hua.

444
00:39:21.854 --> 00:39:24.688
And that is Taher Kaid.
He's the ambassador from Algeria.

445
00:39:24.774 --> 00:39:27.942
Oh, man. Where should I go?
I wanna go all over this place.

446
00:39:28.027 --> 00:39:30.152
Go to Algeria.
See Ben Bella.

447
00:39:30.238 --> 00:39:34.532
Then go to see Mecca and Medina.
I just came from there.

448
00:39:34.616 --> 00:39:36.950
Made my seven circuits
around the Kaaba.

449
00:39:37.036 --> 00:39:40.162
I prayed at sunrise. Two million people.
Pilgrims from all over, man.

450
00:39:40.206 --> 00:39:43.374
Dressed the same.
High and low, the same.

451
00:39:43.459 --> 00:39:47.295
Blond-haired, blue-eyed Muslims,
Arabs, Africans, Indonesians.

452
00:40:02.104 --> 00:40:05.022
Seeing brothers just like us,
praying together, it was beautiful.

453
00:40:05.066 --> 00:40:07.108
I drank water
from the well of Zem Zem.

454
00:40:07.194 --> 00:40:12.239
I prayed in the ancient city of Mena.
I prayed on Mount Arafat.

455
00:40:12.323 --> 00:40:14.740
You shouldn't have quarreled
with Elijah Muhammad.

456
00:40:16.077 --> 00:40:18.286
Walking in their footsteps.

457
00:40:18.372 --> 00:40:19.996
All of us together.

458
00:40:20.081 --> 00:40:22.915
You shouldn't have quarreled
with the Honorable Elijah Muhammad.

459
00:40:23.752 --> 00:40:25.376
What?

460
00:40:26.547 --> 00:40:29.965
You shouldn't have quarreled
with Elijah Muhammad.

461
00:40:30.050 --> 00:40:32.551
Hey, Brother Muhammad,
look here.

462
00:40:36.891 --> 00:40:38.808
Brother Muhammad!

463
00:41:01.042 --> 00:41:03.042
Listen, I'm sorry
to keep you waiting.

464
00:41:17.142 --> 00:41:18.766
Into each life...

465
00:41:18.852 --> 00:41:20.894
a little rain must fall.

466
00:41:20.980 --> 00:41:23.856
And, you know,
every day cannot be sunny.

467
00:41:23.940 --> 00:41:26.607
Every smile is not
a smile of happiness.

468
00:41:26.651 --> 00:41:28.150
And every tear that is shed--

469
00:41:28.195 --> 00:41:30.445
Sonji, Sonji, Sonji.

470
00:41:30.489 --> 00:41:34.241
- What you keep saying my name for?
- 'Cause I love it, girl.

471
00:41:34.326 --> 00:41:36.701
-How long you been working with Herbert?
-About a year.

472
00:41:36.788 --> 00:41:39.664
I sell Muhammad Speaks
over the phone.

473
00:41:39.748 --> 00:41:43.542
- What kind of name is that?
- My father named me after Sonja Henie.

474
00:41:44.670 --> 00:41:46.628
What's your father do?

475
00:41:46.673 --> 00:41:50.801
He was shot in a poker game
when I was two, so he don't do nothing.

476
00:41:50.885 --> 00:41:53.302
And my mother died
when I was eleven.

477
00:41:53.347 --> 00:41:56.223
- Who raised you?
- My godparents.

478
00:41:56.309 --> 00:42:00.311
But I been off on my own
for a long time.

479
00:42:01.438 --> 00:42:03.396
What you doing tomorrow?
Go for a ride with me.

480
00:42:03.482 --> 00:42:05.941
- Oh, no, no. I gotta work.
- I'm gonna square it with Herbert.

481
00:42:06.027 --> 00:42:08.903
